 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  1978BeXU: {+34}S(p,p') with a 40-MeV proton beam on a 80-|mg/cm2 thick 
 34S 2c  sandwich-type 34S target. Scattered protons were momentum-analyzed by  
 34S 3c  an Enge split-pole spectrometer and detected using a 50-cm long        
 34S 4c  position-sensitive proportional counter backed by a plastic            
 34S 5c  scintillator. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, and |p.        

 34S  c  1968Mo22: {+34}S(p,p') with a 12.011-MeV {I17} proton beam from the    
 34S 2c  ONR-CIT tandem accelerator on a CdS target 85%-enriched in {+34}S. The 
 34S 3c  scattered protons were detected using an array of 16 Au-Si surface     
 34S 4c  barrier detectors with FWHM=25 keV at the focal plane of a double      
 34S 5c  focusing magnetic spectrometer. Measured |s(E{-p}). Deduced levels.    

 34S  c  1991Ke09, 1991Kh06: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 318-MeV polarized proton   
 34S 2c  beam from the Los Alamos Meson Physics Facility on a target            
 34S 3c  67.92%-enriched in {+34}S (powder in between thin beryllium foils).    
 34S 4c  Scattered protons were analyzed by the high-resolution spectrometer and
 34S 5c  detected using a standard focal-plane detector. at angles between 5|'  
 34S 6c  and 39|'. Measured differential cross sections and analyzing powers.   

 34S  c  1985Al03: {+34}S(p,p') with a 29.8-MeV proton beam from the Princeton  
 34S 2c  Univeristy AVF cyclotron on 94.3%-enriched {+34}S targets on C         
 34S 3c  backings. Scattered protons were analyzed by a QDDD spectrometer       
 34S 4c  detected using a position-sensitive gas proportional counter with      
 34S 5c  FWHM=20 keV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, and |p.         
 34S  c  1983Iv01: {+34}S(p,p') with a 6-MeV proton beam. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).
 34S  c  1975Al08, 1975Al28: {+34}S(p,p) with a 1-GeV proton beam on a target   
 34S 2c  98.0%-enriched in {+34}S. Scattered protons were detected using a      
 34S 3c  magnetic spectrometer with FWHM=1.6 MeV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).        
 34S  c  1974Gu26: {+34}S(p,p') with 5.4-6.2-MeV proton beams on a thick target 
 34S 2c  97.97%-enriched in {+34}S. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).                      

 34S  c  1972Pl06, 1973Go42: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 24.5-MeV polarized proton  
 34S 2c  beam from the Saclay variable energy cyclctron on Indium sulfide (InS) 
 34S 3c  targets. Scattered protons were detected using cooled Si(Li) detectors.
 34S 4c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q) and aysmmetry(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,  
 34S 5c  and deformation parameters.                                            
 34S  c  1969An35: {+34}S(p,p') with a 6.03-MeV proton beam on an InS target    
 34S 2c  57.17%-enriched in {+34}S. Scattered protons were detected using a     
 34S 3c  Si(Li) detector. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, and |p.     

 34S  c  1999ShZX: {+34}S(p,p') with 160-MeV protons. Measured proton spectra at
 34S 2c  0|'.                                                                   
 34S  c  1999Ma63: systematic discussion of (p,p) and (p,p') on sulfur isotopes.
 34S  c  1985SaZS: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 65-MeV polarized proton beam.        
 34S 2c  Scattered protons were analyzed by a high-resolution magnetic          
 34S 3c  spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-p},|q) and analyzing powers. Deduced the  
 34S 4c  relative signs of neutron and proton transition matrix elements to the 
 34S 5c  2+ state at 3.30 MeV.                                                  
 34S  c  1982Be32, 1982MiZQ: {+34}S(p,p') with 650-MeV protons. Deduced relative
 34S 2c  signs of neutron and proton transition matrix elements to the 2+ state 
 34S 3c  at 3.30 MeV. See 1983Mi25 for distorted wave impulse approximation     
 34S 4c  calculations.                                                          
 34S  c  1980PrZT: {+34}S(p,p') with 6.9-MeV protons. Deduced spin-flip         
 34S 2c  probability in the inelastic scattering to the 2+ state at 2.13 MeV.   
 34S  c  1980Fa07: systematic study of (p,p) and (p,p') with optical model and  
 34S 2c  coupled-channel analysis.                                              
 34S  c  Others: 2005Ko28, 2001Kh17 (inverse kinematics), 1988Za04, 1988Al14,   
 34S 2c  1983Mi25, 1983Ch50.                                                    
